# Zone 1, room 3 (grey box, Phase 1 task 7): tech 3, pogo chain.
# BUILD.md s5, tech 3: "Bounce off a line of enemies or hazards. Taught by a spike pit with Snuffed
# in it"; s15: "a 10-bounce chain across the zone 1 spike pit is possible at 4 bounces per second".
#
# Layout: a hall (18 tiles), a short patch of 3 spikes that a jump or one pogo clears (the safe
# first encounter: a hazard only sends Ash back to the hall's floor), then a tunnel 94 tiles
# (3008 u) long with spikes on its whole floor, then the east hall. The tunnel's ceiling is 64 u
# above the spikes: the player (44 u) can rise 20 u above them and no more, so a jump, a
# dash-jump or the air jump cannot arc over them, and a bounce (794 u/s) rises to the ceiling and
# falls back in 13 frames.
# Stand-ins: the spikes are the line of Snuffed (a hazard is pogo-able as an enemy is); no enemy
# stands in the pit yet.
#
# Why the pit needs pogo: the farthest non-pogo route found (a ground dash-jump, its air jump,
# the air dash and the Ember Toss, searched over every tick that matters) ends 672 u into the
# tunnel, 2336 u short of its far end (tests/replay/zone1/03_control_no_pogo.fixture).
# What the chain asks: a plain chain (a down-strike on each fall, no air jump or air dash between
# bounces) at the dash-jump's 20 u/f bounces every 13 frames (4.6 a second) and crosses in 11
# bounces; at run speed (9 u/f) it takes 26. The air jump or the air dash between bounces
# stretches a stride to 21 to 29 frames and cuts the count to 5 to 9 (a search found it; it is
# tech 4's pogo-dash reset in the next room), so "at least 10 bounces" holds for the plain chain.
room zone1/03_pogo_chain
size 128 34
spawn 96 608
tiles
